# Project 2: Excel Business Formula Integration

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates how Microsoft Excel formulas can be used to solve common business problems through sales data analysis.

The workbook contains a sample sales dataset and applies different Excel functions to calculate sales performance, classify transactions, filter high-value sales, and retrieve product prices.

## Objectives
- Calculate total sales using multiplication.
- Classify sales using IF statements.
- Evaluate performance using AND and OR conditions.
- Filter high-value sales using FILTER.
- Perform conditional calculations using SUMIF, COUNTIF, SUMIFS, COUNTIFS, AVERAGEIF, and AVERAGEIFS.
- Retrieve product prices using VLOOKUP.
- Perform advanced lookups using INDEX and MATCH.
- Combine and split text using Excel text functions.

## Workbook Structure

| Worksheet | Description |
|---|---|
| Sales Data | Main sales dataset and formula calculations |
| High Value Sales | Filtered records with sales above 2,000 |
